        "description": "Expose a port a server in the workspace listens on and get a URL the user can open in the preview panel. This is for dev servers (Vite and the like): static HTML, CSS and JS preview on their own when you write the .html file, so don't start a server for them. Start the server first, in the background and bound to 0.0.0.0 (e.g. `npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173 &`); a server bound to localhost can't be previewed. Don't use port 4747; the static preview has it. Only preview something that serves pages: a library or script with no server has nothing to show."
      },
      "name": "preview",
      "outputSchema": {
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
